---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="SF Ruby News - June 2026"
    description="June 2026 edition of SF Ruby News: Factorial raises $150M at a $2.5B valuation on Rails. Intercom renames the company Fin. Clio crosses $500M ARR. GitLab and Doximity post records. thoughtbot joins the Ruby Alliance. RubyConf Austria draws Dave Thomas and Chad Fowler. SF Ruby meets at PlanetScale June 18."
>
    <section class="relative bg-gradient-to-b from-gray-950 via-gray-900 to-gray-950 text-white overflow-hidden min-h-screen">
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-ruby-950/30"></div>
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10 pt-32 pb-16">

            <!-- Issue Navigation -->
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-8 text-sm">
                <a href="/news/2026-05/" class="text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors flex items-center gap-1">
                    <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" /></svg>
                    May 2026
                </a>
                <span class="text-white/30">Latest issue</span>
            </div>

            <!-- Masthead -->
            <div class="text-center mb-12">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4 justify-center mb-3">
                    <div class="flex-1 max-w-[120px] h-px bg-white/20"></div>
                    <a href="/#news" class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-wider uppercase text-white font-bold hover:text-ruby-400 transition-colors">SF Ruby News</a>
                    <div class="flex-1 max-w-[120px] h-px bg-white/20"></div>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-white/50 tracking-widest uppercase">June 2026</p>
            </div>

            <!-- News Carousel -->
            <div class="relative" id="news-carousel">

                <!-- Page 1 -->
                <div class="news-page" data-page="0">
                    <!-- Headline Story: Factorial Series D -->
                    <div class="mb-10">
                        <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-ruby-500/20 text-ruby-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-4">Funding</span>
                        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold text-white mb-6 leading-tight">Factorial Raises $150M at a $2.5B Valuation</h2>
                        <div class="border-l-2 border-ruby-500/60 pl-6">
                            <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-white/80 leading-relaxed">
                                Barcelona's <strong class="text-white">Factorial</strong>, the HR platform running a Rails backend with 200+ product engineers, closes a $150M Series D led by <strong class="text-white">General Catalyst</strong> and becomes one of Europe's most valuable AI scale-ups.
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mt-4">
                                General Catalyst commits up to an additional $540M through its Customer Value Fund: more than $700M in total. 16,000 businesses across 90 countries, ~2,600 employees, hiring up to 50 people a week. The money funds the shift from HR SaaS to an AI-powered workforce operations platform, plus a new Munich office. <a href="https://tech.eu/2026/06/03/factorial-raises-150m-series-d-at-25b-valuation-to-expand-across-europe/" class="underline hover:text-white/80">Tech.eu has the round details</a>.
                            </p>
                            <div class="mt-4">
                                <p class="text-xs text-white/50">June 3, 2026 · PR Newswire</p>
                            </div>
                            <a href="https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/factorial-raises-150m-series-d-reaches-2-5-billion-valuation-to-become-one-of-the-most-valuable-ai-scale-ups-in-europe-302789074.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 mt-3 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                Read the announcement
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 6H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-4M14 4h6m0 0v6m0-6L10 14" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Divider -->
                    <div class="h-px bg-white/10 mb-10"></div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 1 -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-0 mb-10">
                        <!-- Press: Intercom becomes Fin -->
                        <div class="md:pr-8">
                            <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-3">Press</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Intercom Renames the Company Fin</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">May 12, 2026</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">The 15-year-old company takes its AI agent's name: the corporate entity is now <strong class="text-white/80">Fin</strong>, with Intercom continuing as the help-desk product. Fin crossed $100M ARR, growing 3.5x, inside a $400M+ ARR business, all on the 2M-line Rails monolith. Two days later it shipped <strong class="text-white/80">Fin Operator</strong>: an AI agent that manages the AI agent.</p>
                            <a href="https://www.intercom.com/blog/today-intercom-becomes-fin/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                Read more
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Press: Clio $500M ARR -->
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8 md:pr-8">
                            <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-3">Press</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Clio Crosses $500M ARR</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">May 12, 2026</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">The legal practice platform and longtime Rails shop hits $500M in annual recurring revenue, up from $400M six months prior, serving legal professionals in 130+ countries. CEO Jack Newton frames it as joining "a rare class of profitable, accelerating AI platforms." Follows the $1B vLex acquisition and a $5B valuation.</p>
                            <a href="https://www.clio.com/about/press/clio-500-million-arr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                Read more
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Earnings: GitLab Q1 FY27 -->
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8">
                            <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-3">Earnings</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">GitLab: $264M Quarter, Agentic Tailwinds</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">June 2, 2026</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">Rails Foundation Core member reports Q1 FY2027 revenue of $264.2M (+23%), 14% non-GAAP operating margin, $149M operating cash flow, and 117% net retention. CEO Bill Staples: <strong class="text-white/80">"The agentic era is creating structural tailwinds for GitLab."</strong></p>
                            <a href="https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260602438182/en/GitLab-Reports-First-Quarter-Fiscal-Year-2027-Financial-Results" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                Read more
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 2 -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-0 mb-6">
                        <div class="md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit">Earnings</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Doximity: $645M Year, 800K Prescribers</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">SF-based Rails Foundation Core member closes FY2026 with $644.9M revenue (+13%) and $317.5M free cash flow (+19%). A record 800K+ active prescribers use its workflow tools; nearly half already use its clinical AI, with prompts per user nearly doubling from January to April.</p>
                                <a href="https://press.doximity.com/articles/doximity-announces-fourth-quarter-and-fiscal-year-2026-financial-results" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8 md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-violet-500/20 text-violet-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit">Release</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Checkr Launches Profiles: Identity That Travels</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">SF background-check platform ($2.2B valuation, Rails) ships portable verified identity: identity verification, background checks, and credential validation in a shareable profile that individuals own. Built against AI-era fraud; per Checkr's research, 62% of managers believe people now fake identity better than organizations detect it.</p>
                                <a href="https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/checkr-launches-profiles-giving-people-a-verified-identity-that-travels-with-them-302756790.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-violet-400 hover:text-violet-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-ruby-500/20 text-ruby-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit">Event</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">SF Ruby Meetup, June @ PlanetScale</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">Thursday June 18, 5pm, 108 Natoma St. Jeremy Evans on "Implementing Core Set," Alan Ridlehoover's "Indispensable: What Human Computers Can Teach Human Programmers," plus a PlanetScale talk and interest circles. Hosted with Sam Lambert. 108+ RSVPs.</p>
                                <a href="https://lu.ma/ltipgvuh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                    RSVP on Luma
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Hiring strip -->
                    <div class="mt-4 mb-6 border border-white/10 rounded-lg px-6 py-4 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center gap-3 md:gap-6">
                        <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit shrink-0">Hiring</span>
                        <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed flex-1">Fresh Ruby roles on the board, every listing re-verified this week: <strong class="text-white/80">Gusto</strong> (Staff, Payments/Risk), <strong class="text-white/80">Superconductor</strong> (Principal Rails), <strong class="text-white/80">Koah Labs</strong> (Backend, Product, Platform), <strong class="text-white/80">Omada Health</strong>, <strong class="text-white/80">CompanyCam</strong>, plus open roles at Thatch, Persona, Chime, Patch, Reset, and Finta.</p>
                        <a href="/jobs" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-amber-400 hover:text-amber-300 transition-colors shrink-0">
                            Browse all jobs
                            <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Page 2 -->
                <div class="news-page hidden" data-page="1">
                    <!-- Headline Story: RubyConf Austria -->
                    <div class="mb-10">
                        <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-ruby-500/20 text-ruby-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-4">Event</span>
                        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold text-white mb-6 leading-tight">RubyConf Austria Draws the Legends to Vienna</h2>
                        <div class="border-l-2 border-ruby-500/60 pl-6">
                            <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-white/80 leading-relaxed">
                                <strong class="text-white">Dave Thomas</strong> opens with "Start Writing Ruby." <strong class="text-white">Chad Fowler</strong> answers with "This is What We've Been Training For." One panel seats Fowler, <strong class="text-white">José Valim</strong>, <strong class="text-white">Obie Fernandez</strong>, and <strong class="text-white">Armin Ronacher</strong> on the same stage.
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mt-4">
                                22 talks over three days: Bozhidar Batsov asks "RuboCop 2.0: Where do we go now?", Charles Nutter runs a JRuby workshop, Marco Roth delivers "Herb &amp; ReActionView: Mid-2026 Progress Update," and Carmine Paolino argues "Ruby Is the Best Language for Building AI Web Apps," the same case he made in Sofia two weeks earlier.
                            </p>
                            <div class="mt-4">
                                <p class="text-xs text-white/50">May 29–31, 2026 · Vienna, Austria</p>
                            </div>
                            <a href="https://rubyevents.org/events/rubyconf-austria-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 mt-3 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                See the full lineup
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 6H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-4M14 4h6m0 0v6m0-6L10 14" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Divider -->
                    <div class="h-px bg-white/10 mb-10"></div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 1 -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-0 mb-10">
                        <!-- Event: Balkan Ruby -->
                        <div class="md:pr-8">
                            <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-ruby-500/20 text-ruby-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-3">Event</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Balkan Ruby 2026 in Sofia</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">May 15–16, 2026</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">12 talks heavy on AI and Rails internals: Jean Boussier on multiprocessing as the most efficient way to serve Rails apps, Marco Roth on HTML-aware ERB, Vladimir Dementyev (Evil Martians) with "Drop your app/services!", and a PostgreSQL-to-SQLite migration story from production.</p>
                            <a href="https://rubyevents.org/events/balkan-ruby-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                See the lineup
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Event: Brighton Ruby -->
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8 md:pr-8">
                            <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-ruby-500/20 text-ruby-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-3">Event</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Brighton Ruby Returns June 25</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">June 25, 2026</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">The long-running single-day UK conference returns with 11 talks: Rachael Wright-Munn's "Your First Open-Source Contribution," David Paluy's "LLM Telemetry as a First-Class Rails Concern" (the same talk that ran at Blue Ridge — LLM telemetry is having a moment), and Brooke Kuhlmann's Hanami + htmx app for e-ink devices.</p>
                            <a href="https://rubyevents.org/events/brighton-ruby-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                See the lineup
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Release: Shopify Summer '26 Edition -->
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8">
                            <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-violet-500/20 text-violet-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-3">Release</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Shopify Summer '26: Horizon Themes, AI Blocks</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">May 2026</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">Rails Foundation Core member ships 150+ changes: the Horizon theme system with 10 free themes and AI block generation via Shopify Magic, up to 50% faster cart and checkout, a ground-up POS v10, Sidekick answering plain-English questions over ShopifyQL, and Payments in 16 new countries.</p>
                            <a href="https://www.shopify.com/editions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-violet-400 hover:text-violet-300 transition-colors">
                                Read more
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 2 -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-0 mb-6">
                        <div class="md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit">Press</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Persona Clears FedRAMP Moderate</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">The SF identity unicorn ($2B valuation, Rails backend) earns FedRAMP Moderate Authorization as the only identity-verification provider in the FedRAMP 20x Phase 2 pilot. Federal agencies can now deploy Persona directly via the FedRAMP Marketplace and Carahsoft.</p>
                                <a href="https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260521233540/en/Persona-Achieves-FedRAMP-Moderate-Authorization-Giving-Federal-Agencies-Modern-Identity-Verification" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8 md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit">Funding</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Great Question Raises $13M Series A</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">The Bay Area UX research platform (YC W21, Rails + React) raises from Inovia Capital to expand its AI-driven research tools. Customers include ServiceNow, Brex, Canva, and Asana.</p>
                                <a href="https://greatquestion.co/blog/series-a" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-ruby-500/20 text-ruby-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit">AI + Ruby</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Natural: Agentic Payments, Built on Rails</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">The SF startup building payment infrastructure for AI agents (wallets, pay, request, and credit across banking and stablecoins) runs Ruby on Rails under the hood. Out of stealth with a $9.8M seed, and currently hiring 15 engineering roles.</p>
                                <a href="https://www.natural.co/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 3 -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-0 mb-6">
                        <!-- Press: RubyGems security -->
                        <div class="md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit">Press</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">RubyGems Repels a Supply-Chain Attack</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">Thousands of attacker-controlled accounts flooded the registry with tens of thousands of malicious packages (May 11). RubyGems suspended new signups, yanked 500+ packages, shipped WAF and rate-limiting fixes with Fastly, and reopened registrations within five days. The week the Ruby Alliance launched, its reason to exist made the case in production.</p>
                                <a href="https://thehackernews.com/2026/05/rubygems-suspends-new-signups-after.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more
